 "result_text": "I fixed the call-order bug in `nose2/suite.py`. I didn't run the issue's gist or add a test for this case, so the fix itself is untested.\n\n**Cause:** `LayerSuite.run` ran its layer `setUp` without first tearing down the class fixtures left over from the preceding ordinary `unittest` test case. That class's `tearDownClass` only fired when the first layer test started, after the layer's `setUp`. That is the mixed-up ordering in the issue.\n\n**Fix:** `LayerSuite.run` now tears down the previous class and module fixtures before it sets up the layer.\n\n**Tests:** The layer tests pass (8 of 8). The functional suite has one failure, `test_loadtests_plugin.test_package`. I think it's unrelated to this change, because it fails on a `load_tests` test-name regex mismatch. The rerun that was meant to confirm it also fails without my change only printed that same failure count, and I didn't check which test failed there.",
